From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pankaj Gupta <quic_gpankaj@quicinc.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Jan 2023 18:48:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Revert "msm: kgsl: Call dma_buf_unmap_attachment() early"

This reverts msm-5.10 commit b84bd97e37f8ac3a0f3194ebcbb1fa962e42cd73.

Warnings for direct dma clients during cache operations are now being
suppressed by dma-buf driver. Instead of doing dma_buf_unmap_attachment
early if we do it in destroy path, it helps in saving cycles and
improving performance during app launch. This is also helping in fixing
EGL image corruption issue.

Change-Id: Ic66dd3b66136318abf59685f95fee17890377fd4
Signed-off-by: Pankaj Gupta <quic_gpankaj@quicinc.com>
(cherry picked from commit 085a050df7ac65e2bd2805e71cd9eed40ca34c74)
---
 kgsl.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kgsl.c b/kgsl.c
index 8a1209c..5c68788 100644
--- a/kgsl.c
+++ b/kgsl.c
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /*
  * Copyright (c) 2008-2021, The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
- * Copyright (c) 2022 Qualcomm Innovation Center, Inc. All rights reserved.
+ * Copyright (c) 2022-2023 Qualcomm Innovation Center, Inc. All rights reserved.
  */
 
 #include <uapi/linux/sched/types.h>
@@ -341,6 +341,7 @@ static void kgsl_destroy_ion(struct kgsl_memdesc *memdesc)
 
 	if (meta != NULL) {
 		remove_dmabuf_list(meta);
+		dma_buf_unmap_attachment(meta->attach, memdesc->sgt, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 		dma_buf_detach(meta->dmabuf, meta->attach);
 		dma_buf_put(meta->dmabuf);
 		kfree(meta);
@@ -3268,8 +3269,6 @@ static int kgsl_setup_dma_buf(struct kgsl_device *device,
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	dma_buf_unmap_attachment(attach, sg_table, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
-
 	meta->table = sg_table;
 	entry->priv_data = meta;
 	entry->memdesc.sgt = sg_table;
